Translate a strategic plan into tasks, readiness, and feedback at shorter timescales (@mine-operating-plan: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #source "../sources/SME-Mining-Engineering-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y1TJWVHWWCYTYAKZKMAEAVX25", #source "../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "../../../../gaia/earth/geology/structures/Stress-strain-and-deformation-history.lingua#r_4TM454JHNMW1X3RF37NBDRXTXT") { r_28TW1F4Z2GG8HTSTF4N3D8SPXC
**Read:** [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the complete planning, layout, operating, and capacity context; [SME Mining Engineering Handbook — Peter Darling, third edition](../sources/SME-Mining-Engineering-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y1TJWVHWWCYTYAKZKMAEAVX25), the complete relevant planning/operations chapters; [Introduction to Mining Engineering — Penn State MNG 230](../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2), the full lifecycle and system connections.

A long-range plan aggregates activities over periods and supports strategic choices. An operating plan needs physically sequenced work, access, prepared faces, equipment, people, supplies, services, maintenance, and changing conditions. Disaggregating a target number does not create that readiness.

Separate scheduled capacity, available capacity, actual operating time, delays, rehandling, and measured output. Define event and state records consistently before comparing production with plan. A missed target can reflect an incorrect assumption, unprepared work, constrained service, measurement discrepancy, or several interacting causes.

Feedback should connect observations to the model and decision they can change. Updated grade/ground/plant information can revise destinations, sequence, or investigation needs. Preserve actual deviations and handoff conditions rather than overwriting the original plan or treating every difference as operator failure.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete published/teaching operating period from a strategic target through prepared tasks, dependencies, resources, events, measurements, and revisions. Independently check one capacity/time/material account and explain the limiting interface. Compare two responses to a consequential deviation and the evidence supporting them.

Read full planning, layout, and operation sections. Continue through [Distinguish force, stress, strain, and the history producing a structure](../../../../gaia/earth/geology/structures/Stress-strain-and-deformation-history.lingua#r_4TM454JHNMW1X3RF37NBDRXTXT) for shared stress/strain foundations before developing the ground model, excavation response, support, and monitoring that constrain real extraction sequences.

**Continue:** [Distinguish force, stress, strain, and the history producing a structure](../../../../gaia/earth/geology/structures/Stress-strain-and-deformation-history.lingua#r_4TM454JHNMW1X3RF37NBDRXTXT).

**Return:** [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).
